    "rationale": "URAT1 is located on the apical membrane of proximal tubular cells and mediates reabsorption of filtered urate from the tubular lumen. Biallelic SLC22A12 loss reduces urate reabsorption, causing hypouricemia and high fractional urate excretion; renal hypouricemia is associated with exercise-induced acute kidney injury. Strongest alternative resolved: ABCG2 participates in urate secretion, but the stem supplies biallelic SLC22A12 loss and increased fractional urate excretion. URAT1 is the apical proximal-tubule reabsorptive transporter encoded by SLC22A12, so loss directly impairs urate reabsorption."
